 "about_text": "Contemporary HEIS is a Tokyo gallery founded in 2012 to specialize in contemporary art. It introduces young Japanese artists to audiences in Japan and abroad through exhibitions and international art fairs, while also mounting shows that revisit postwar Japanese movements such as Art Informel, Neo-Dada and Kyushu-ha. The gallery additionally deals in works by Mono-ha artists. Rather than confining itself to a single genre, Contemporary HEIS centers its program on abstract expression, building relationships with artists and collectors across a range of practices and generations.",
